      },
      {
       "kind": "add",
       "text": "",
       "newLine": 20
      },
      {
       "kind": "add",
       "text": "Each client IP gets a token bucket. Over the limit, the API answers",
       "newLine": 21
      },
      {
       "kind": "add",
       "text": "`429 Too Many Requests` with a `Retry-After` header in whole seconds.",
       "newLine": 22
      },
      {
       "kind": "add",
       "text": "",
       "newLine": 23
      },
      {
       "kind": "add",
       "text": "Limits are per process and kept in memory: two replicas allow twice the rate,",
       "newLine": 24
      },
      {
       "kind": "add",
       "text": "and a restart forgets every bucket. Behind a reverse proxy all clients share",
       "newLine": 25
      },
      {
       "kind": "add",
       "text": "the proxy's IP, so put the limiter at the proxy or trust a forwarded header",
       "newLine": 26
      },
      {
       "kind": "add",
       "text": "there first.",
       "newLine": 27
      }
     ]
    }
